  "description": "Provide the shared measurement protocol and acceptance-summary support that independently runnable CPU benchmark families consume.\n\n## Background\n\nThe existing coding comparison runners, offline tuning system and exclusive host lock are canonical. This task specifies reusable statistical and receipt rules; family comparator builds, baseline campaigns and consumer profiling are separate work. The measurement contract states the normative requirements without pretending that numeric experiment settings are already frozen.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: Publish a versioned executable protocol satisfying the [measurement contract](dev/active/1a379447-zen3-cpu-performance/measurement-contract.md), with an explicit schema for independently frozen cell addenda. Store the protocol and schema under the owning development directory and pin immutable artifact snapshots by content digest in emitted receipts; Git revisions are optional navigation metadata.\n\n- [hard] REQ-02: Define paired/interleaved A/B sampling and bootstrap confidence intervals for the ratio of medians, the resampling unit, cache-state and outlier policies, family-wise multiple-comparison treatment, independent holdout confirmation and bounded search/stop rules. Freeze shared numerical settings and require applicable family-specific settings before each confirmatory trial.\n\n- [hard] REQ-03: Define family-specific worthwhile-effect and complexity-budget fields, with justified improvement and non-regression equivalence margins. Do not impose a blanket 15% or 1.5x threshold; retain hard correctness and mandatory benchmarking. Distinguish exploratory pilots from confirmation and prevent failed confirmation data from being silently relabeled or discarded.\n\n- [hard] REQ-04: Extend the canonical receipt/acceptance tooling to check required provenance, protocol/addendum identity, sample budgets, confidence-bound decisions, unavailable cells and complete negative results. Exercise pass, fail, inconclusive, missing-content, digest-mismatch and resumed-run cases, including metadata-only Git commits and unrelated edits between sessions with deterministic fixtures and a bounded release smoke receipt; no production performance change is included.\n\n- [hard] REQ-05: Verify canonical quiet-host locking, append-only execution logs, checkpoint/resume, runtime topology/affinity and worker reporting in the shared runner. Include separate kernel/whole-consumer and single-core/multicore metrics, conservative/tuned/native build identities and conversion costs in the schema without requiring all family campaigns to run here.\n\n- [hard] REQ-06: Define matched-algorithm versus fastest quality-compatible decoder cell schemas, including input/code identity, precision, schedule, stopping, batching, memory and BER/FER confidence intervals. Actual comparator compatibility and build choices remain family survey outputs.\n\n- [hard] REQ-07: Commit the reviewed protocol, schema, tooling validation and linked reproducible smoke evidence. Numeric family settings may be supplied later by addenda, but every unresolved required setting makes its cell non-confirmatory rather than implicitly defaulted.\n\n## Notes\n\nProvenance and resume follow @/inv/behavioral-evidence-validity: content identities of producing code, executables, configuration and inputs are authoritative; Git-object availability, commit ancestry and repository-wide clean/dirty status are not acceptance conditions. Freeze the content snapshot in the append-only execution record before measurements and cite a distinct pilot receipt by digest.\n\nThis is measurement infrastructure only. It does not build every comparator, profile every consumer, tune production dispatch or establish a claimed speedup.\n\n",
